    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed storage for a GWAS genotype dataset of 8587 samples and 7267829 variants, including per-chromosome file sizing.",
    "rationale": "The .bed binary format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Total .bed size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome .bed size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (281272). The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the dataset; for a standard human GWAS this is 25 (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT), but this is a dataset-structure assumption to confirm in the lab.",
